<description>
Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.

Input structure
The grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the
cross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form
the surrounding filler or separators.
Rule
Find that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by
the pair, and return the induced subgrid.
Key insight
The target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask
whose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after
deleting unused rows and columns.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "unique two-color mask whose pixels fill the cross product of its active rows and active columns",
  "transform": "delete every row and column not touched by that mask, preserving the induced two-color subgrid",
  "grid_shape": "active mask rows x active mask columns"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, 19-28 rows/cols
  colors: 4-5 distinct colors total; exactly 2 form the hidden image (target pair), 2-3 are filler/separator
  structure: |
    NxN arrangement of square blocks (N=3-4, block_size=3-5) containing
    ONLY the target pair colors, separated by filler rows/cols.
    Row/col separator layout is symmetric (same pattern for rows and cols).
    Border padding: 2-5 rows/cols on each side (top/bottom may differ).
    Internal separators: 1-3 rows/cols wide (uniform within a grid).
    Formula: grid_size = N*block_size + (N-1)*internal_sep + border_top + border_bottom
  hidden_image:
    occupies: exactly the cross-product of its active rows x active cols (key constraint)
    bg_color: majority color in output (fills ~80-86% of output area)
    fg_color: minority, forms a 1-pixel-wide connected shape (path, branching, or closed loop)
    fg_fraction: 0.14-0.22 of output area
    connectivity: single 4-connected component; spans all N block-rows and all N block-cols
  separator_region:
    filled_by: only non-target colors (randomly mixed)
    ensures: no other color pair satisfies the cross-product condition
  uniqueness: exactly one pair satisfies pixels == active_rows * active_cols with 0 < active < grid_size

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Choose N (3-4), block_size (3-5), internal_sep (1-3), border_top/bottom (>=internal_sep, 2-5)
    - Pick 4 distinct colors; assign 2 as target_pair (bg+fg), 2+ as filler
    - Build the output (N*block_size square): fill with bg, draw a 1-pixel-wide connected fg shape spanning all block-rows and block-cols
    - Construct input grid by inserting separator rows/cols of width internal_sep between block groups, plus border padding
    - Fill all separator cells (sep_row x any_col UNION any_row x sep_col) with random mix of filler colors
    - Verify uniqueness: confirm no other pair of input colors satisfies the cross-product condition (guaranteed by construction since filler colors span all rows/cols via separators)
```
</generation_spec>
